# Dantooine, the Khoonda Plains and Khoonda (TSL, 003EBO, 601DAN, 602DAN):
# the galaxy map to Dantooine, Bao-Dur on the Exile's lightsaber, ashore
# with Bao-Dur and Kreia (DSimpson: Bao-Dur for the sensors); Dillan's
# greeting, the battered droid ([Computer] diagnosed, [Repair]ed, and the
# mechanic [Persuade]d the Exile is no Jedi), the landing pad's containers (one locked,
# Bao-Dur's Security; the "{Blast}" cylinder is left shut, see below), into
# Khoonda: Suulru's vaporator (helped), Administrator Adare (the Ebon Hawk
# owned, the Force's guidance, Vrook to be found first: the sublevel's
# permission), Berun, and out to
# Saedhe by the cave (the atmospheric sensors asked after: DSimpson takes
# his quest, not Berun's evidence). Starts from Telos's last checkpoint:
#   kjk playthrough tsl @telos_done data/routes/tsl/dantooine_khoonda.route --god
say [Repair] Diagnose the droid # the old HK unit's remains in the cargo
say [Repair] Take the vocabulator # hold: HK-47's rebuilding begun, the
say Step away.       # vocabulator from Peragus fitted
use DrdParts
talk
say As many as want to come with us # aboard after Telos (Bao-Dur's talk on
                     # the Exile's lightsaber and his work on T3 as the
                     # party walks), Kreia's talks
say They're my friends, not my followers # (DSimpson's light answers):
say Does the fact they obey me upset you # those who follow us, then her
say No, what?        # past ([Intelligence]), her story's vision after
say They are my friends, not tools
say I had other questions
say Kreia, what are you
say [Intelligence] Then what were you?
say I still wish to hear the story
use kreia
talk
say Never mind. I'll be going now # her word after the vision (1000 XP)
talk
say Let's play pazaak # Atton: a hand of pazaak, Republic Senate rules,
say Let's just play for practice, then # for practice (his past waits on
use atton            # more of his influence)
talk
pazaak
use Galaxymap
travel 0             # Dantooine (planetary.2da); Bao-Dur's lightsaber talk
                     # played as the party walked aboard
party 1,6            # Bao-Dur and Kreia
to tr_leave          # the ramp: the party screen, accepted
module 601dan
talk                 # Dillan's greeting off the ship
use olddroid         # the battered protocol droid: its diagnostic and repair
talk
use MilLowPlstcCylin@2 # the landing pad's cylinders
use MilLowPlstcCylin@3
use MilLowPlstcCylin@4
use CivilFootLker    # the Ithorian's footlocker (DSimpson: "goodies")
say I'd like to see your wares # Akkere's stall by Khoonda's door: the
use npc_akkere       # droid's part HK-47 will need (DSimpson: buy it
talk                 # here), and a computer spike for the Enclave's
buy hkpart03         # storage room
buy g_i_progspike01 3
leader 1             # the locked cylinder by Khoonda's wall (DC 18):
unlock MilHighPlstcCylin # Bao-Dur's Security
use MilHighPlstcCylin
leader player
# Left shut: the pad's "Plasteel Cylinder{Med, Blast}" (MilMidPlstcCylin),
# which no key opens (KeyRequired, no key) and DSimpson mines open: TSL's
# mine set on a container is not built (the sim's is a door's).
exit To_602          # Khoonda's front door
module 602dan
say I'll see what I can do. # Suulru: Jorran's missing modulator
use npc_suulru
talk
say I came in that ship, yes. # Administrator Adare
say I'd prefer if you keep that quiet
say The Force seems to have guided me here
say He didn't send for me, but I would like to meet with him
say I will make it my first priority. # the sublevel's permission
use npc_terena
talk
say Who are you?      # Berun (DSimpson's light way): his doubts of
say It sounds like you don't approve of him # Zherron, and a look into
say Can't anyone do something about it # him asked of us
say So what could I do to help
say I'll be going now
use npc_berun
talk
# BLOCKER: Zherron's kinrath job and Berun's message for Dopak left (and
# the job's reward, in dantooine_cave, and the salvagers' will, given
# Daraala instead in dantooine_enclave): every walk back from his post makes
# for a corner of the way at the militia desk (-6.9, -15.3), where the free
# floor is a diagonal channel between the desk's sloped nonwalk foot and
# the wall, about a body wide; the walk reaches the corner and makes for
# the next straight across the desk's foot, its sidesteps bring it back to
# the corner, and the party's floating remote stands in the channel's
# mouth (SKIPPED.md).
exit To_601
module 601dan
use MilLowPlstcCylin@1 # by the crashed speeder
say What are you doing out here? # Saedhe: the missing atmospheric sensors
say I'll see what I can do.
use npc_saedhe
talk
use MilLowPlstcCylin@5 # beside him
save dantooine_plains
